Now it's all verified on a real stress corpus. The results:

Memory stays flat at ~51 MB while scanning a 318 MB corpus that includes a single 320 MB log file and a spreadsheet with 50,000 matching cells. 
    That's the whole scaling story in one number — peak RSS is bounded by streaming + capping, not by corpus size or any individual file's size. 
